        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "He wears a red hat and a blue coat, carrying an old suitcase. A tag around his neck says, “Please look after this bear.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "This is Paddington Bear, one of the most "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "beloved",
            "ref": "v-beloved"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " characters in children’s books."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Sixty-seven years ago, British writer Michael Bond "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "introduced",
            "ref": "v-introduce"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " Paddington to the world. In the story, the bear arrives in London alone and meets the kind Brown family. They take him home and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "treat",
            "ref": "v-treat"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " him as family."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Bond once bought a teddy bear from a London store as a gift for his wife. He named it Paddington because he lived near Paddington Station. That little bear later became the star of his books."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Bond wrote more than 20 stories about Paddington. These books have sold over 35 million "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "copies",
            "ref": "v-copy"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " around the world and have been translated into 40 languages. Paddington also became famous in movies and TV shows. Many toys and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "souvenirs",
            "ref": "v-souvenir"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " were made based on him."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Why do people love Paddington so much? It’s not just because he looks cute. More importantly, he is polite, kind, and always "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "optimistic",
            "ref": "v-optimistic"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". No matter what trouble he meets, he stays positive. As Bond said, “He has the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "naivety",
            "zh": "天真"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of a child and the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "sophistication",
            "zh": "成熟"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of an adult.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Paddington is a timeless character. He helps many children fall in love with reading."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
